.ds q \N'34'
.TH fastcompmgr 1
.SH NAME
fastcompmgr \- a _fast_ compositor for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B fastcompmgr [\-d display] [\-r radius] [\-o opacity] [\-l left-offset] [\-t top-offset] [\-m opacity] [\-i opacity] [\-e opacity] [\-I step] [\-O step] [\-D milliseconds] [\-cCfFS] [\-\-shadow-red value] [\-\-shadow-green value] [\-\-shadow-blue value] [\-\-refresh-rate Hz] [\-\-print-stats]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastcompmgr
is a compositor based on Dana Jansens' version of xcompmgr (which itself was
written by Keith Packard) and on an early verion of Christopher Jeffrey's
compton. It includes many improvements over the original
xcompmgr, including window frame opacity, inactive window transparency,
and shadows on argb windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d\ display
Specifies the display to manage.
.TP
.BI \-r\ radius
Specifies the blur radius for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-o\ opacity
Specifies the opacity for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-l\ left-offset
Specifies the left offset for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-t\ top-offset
Specifies the top offset for client-side shadows.
.TP
.BI \-m\ opacity
Specifies opacity for menu, dropdown-menu, popup-menu, and combo windows.
.TP
.BI \-I\ fade-in-step
Specifies the opacity change between steps while fading in.
.TP
.BI \-O\ fade-out-step
Specifies the opacity change between steps while fading out.
.TP
.BI \-D\ fade-delta
Specifies the time (in milliseconds) between steps in a fade.
.TP
.BI \-c
Enable client-side shadows on windows.
Shadows are not drawn on menus, popup menus, dropdown menus, combo-box
popups, or tooltips; those window types expose only an oversized rect with no
shape information and would render as a transparent box around the popup.
.TP
.BI \-f
When \-c is specified, enables a smooth fade effect for transient windows like
menus, and for all windows on hide and restore events.
.TP
.BI \-C
When \-c is specified, attempts to avoid painting shadows on panels and docks.
.TP
.BI \-F
When \-f is specified, also enables the fade effect when windows change their
opacity, as with transset(1).
.TP
.BI \-i\ opacity
Specifies inactive window transparency. (0.0 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-e\ opacity
Specifies window frame transparency. (0.0 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-S
Enables synchronous operation. Useful for debugging; normal operation is asynchronous.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Prints usage information.
.TP
.BI \-\-shadow-red\ value
Specifies shadow red intensity. (0.0 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-shadow-green\ value
Specifies shadow green intensity. (0.0 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-shadow-blue\ value
Specifies shadow blue intensity. (0.0 - 1.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh-rate\ Hz
Overrides the display refresh rate. Zero selects XRandR autodetection.
.TP
.B \-\-print-stats
Prints one line of rendering statistics per second to standard error.
.SH BUGS
Bugs may be reported to https://github.com/ztancrell/fastcompmgr
.SH AUTHORS
xcompmgr, originally written by Keith Packard, with contributions from
Matthew Allum, Eric Anholt, Dan Doel, Thomas Luebking, Matthew Hawn,
Ely Levy, Phil Blundell, and Carl Worth.
Compton by Christopher Jeffrey, based on Dana Jansens' original work.
fastcompmgr by Tycho Kirchner.
